  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 1.1.4, 'Essential processes of national digital health implementations'. A left-to-right flow runs DIGITAL HEALTH STRATEGY → INVESTMENT ROADMAP → ENTERPRISE ARCHITECTURE → APPLICATION WITH INTERVENTIONS → SCALE, INSTITUTIONALIZE AND SUSTAIN, with a feedback arrow from scaling back to applications. Inputs feed in from above: national health priorities (into the strategy), the national inventory of digital assets (exchanged with the roadmap and architecture) and health-programme-specific needs. Governance mechanisms and a data use culture support from below, and the digital maturity of the country informs the strategy. A shaded region labelled DIIG encloses the architecture, applications and scaling steps — the part this guide covers. At the bottom sit the national eHealth strategy building blocks: leadership and governance; strategy and investment; legislation, policy and compliance; workforce; infrastructure; standards and interoperability; and services and applications.",
